{"hash":"d3b1f4246eeedc28","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":85.511,"said":"Nandi waits here, always facing his Lord, and the steps beyond him lead down to the sanctum. Before we go down, the story’s last scene. Daruki, alone now, prayed to Parvati, the goddess who had once blessed her. Parvati listened, and promised: ‘I will protect your race.’ Then, the Purana says, Shiva and Parvati had a gentle quarrel, each of them bound by a promise. Shiva smiled and told her, ‘Do as you please.’ Parvati laughed, and found a way for both promises to hold. Shiva’s word would come true at the end of the age; until then, Daruki would rule over the rakshasas, and their families could live on in the forest. Shiva was pleased. ‘Then I too will stay in this forest,’ he said, ‘to protect my devotees.’ And so the Lord who rose from the earth to save a merchant remained here as a Jyotirlinga called Nageshwara, Lord of the Nagas, the serpents, and the goddess came to be known as Nageshwari. Below, you will see her too, just behind him. Now go down the steps, slowly. The sanctum lies below the hall.\n\nDid you know? The Purana adds a prophecy: in a later age a devoted king, Virasena, would sail to this forest in a fish-shaped boat to worship Nageshwara.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1017},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1033,"end":1172}],"words":[[0.098,0.433,0,5],[0.543,0.349,6,11],[0.903,0.325,12,16],[1.48,0.433,18,24],[1.925,0.385,25,31],[2.322,0.204,32,35],[2.538,0.361,36,40],[3.091,0.18,42,45],[3.283,0.096,46,49],[3.391,0.397,50,55],[3.8,0.349,56,62],[4.161,0.18,63,66],[4.353,0.276,67,71],[4.641,0.264,72,76],[4.918,0.084,77,79],[5.014,0.096,80,83],[5.122,0.625,84,91],[6.659,0.433,93,99],[7.103,0.12,100,102],[7.236,0.192,103,105],[7.44,0.409,106,110],[8.137,0.108,112,115],[8.257,0.529,116,123],[8.798,0.349,124,128],[9.159,0.433,129,134],[10.457,0.709,136,142],[11.394,0.373,144,149],[11.779,0.349,150,153],[12.32,0.288,155,161],[12.62,0.12,162,164],[12.7